{
  "$comment": [
    "What the engine and the Android application (seawolves-android) exchange by name. Both sides check themselves",
    "against this file: tests/app_contract here (the engine sources say exactly this), the application's",
    "tests/engine_contract (its Java and its interface scripts accept and send exactly this). Change a name in",
    "the engine: change it here in the same commit; the application's host checks then fail until it follows.",
    "engine_commands: what the main loop's command dispatcher accepts (main.cpp; an unknown one is an error log),",
    "  a prefix ends in ':' (or a tab), anything else is the whole command; the value says who sends it",
    "  (ui = the UI library in the engine, app = the activity's mailbox, GameActivity.queueMobileAction).",
    "hud_host_input: HUD actions the engine hands to the activity (onUiHudInput) and the values each may carry.",
    "host_actions: UI actions without an engine command (onUiAction nodes, Bindings::SendHost).",
    "state_channels: what each host writes into the UI (EngineUi/StormUi setState) and the UI consumes.",
    "settings: the settings screen's application keys, the facts the host reports beside them, and the debug",
    "  overrides of a debuggable build with the values the screen offers (-1 = the preset decides).",
    "script_events: events the engine raises that the application's interface scripts (mobile-ui/PROGRAM)",
    "  handle, with the arguments the engine passes.",
    "jni.natives: Java native methods per class of org.stormengine.port, each exported as Java_..._<class>_<name>.",
    "jni.upcalls: Java methods the engine looks up, class (of org.stormengine.port), name and JNI descriptor."
  ],
  "engine_commands": {
    "audiofocus:": "app",
    "back": "ui+app",
    "camera:": "app",
